Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:11:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Two faults that the full suite found on the tip of this
 seat's deliveries since main's 0e637ea9e (cld-advisor; after C11)

The full suite on a fresh clone of C15's tip: 6 failed, 8,677 passed, 74 skipped. Four of the six are known:
three ask that every gate pass, and the count of landings is past 40; one (B1426's) fails in a fresh clone at
main's head, by main's word. Two were new, and this patch mends both.

ONE. B1862's tripwire for old corrected forms read the rows of B1905, six readers' rows each quoting a verdict
line as it stood at a15516d43, and found an old form (E3) in them. It fails at main's head too, on main's own
hand-over copy of the same file; card C13 added the arc's copy. The rows are a reader's report by their kind, and
the tripwire already leaves readers' reports unread. The arc's copy is added to its list of what is not read,
under a dated note (main's hand-over copy left the tree with C13's first patch, built again on main's 204ee91ed).

TWO. The ledger of walls' test that its generator leaves no compiled file beside B1905's script looked for the
folder of compiled files at all. pytest writes that folder for the arc's lock, which stands in the same place,
so in a run of the suite it was there. The test now looks for a compiled copy of B1905's script, which is what
the generator must not leave; the line as it stood is kept in a dated note.

THIS SEAT'S OWN FAULTS: both new failures came with card C13 (its first two patches), and the runs at its
sending chose its test files by what they read, and not the whole suite. They are mended here, at the end of the
chain, and not by sending C13 again.

The two tests, with the arc's lock: 31 passed (and the ledger's test with pytest's caches on: 6 passed).
---
 .../test_b1862_the_audits_first_corrections.py             | 7 ++++++-
 tests/test_ledger_of_walls.py                              | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/frontier/B1862_the_audits_first_corrections/verification/test_b1862_the_audits_first_corrections.py b/frontier/B1862_the_audits_first_corrections/verification/test_b1862_the_audits_first_corrections.py
index c8b972d57..707cfb886 100644
--- a/frontier/B1862_the_audits_first_corrections/verification/test_b1862_the_audits_first_corrections.py
+++ b/frontier/B1862_the_audits_first_corrections/verification/test_b1862_the_audits_first_corrections.py
@@ -260,7 +260,12 @@ NOT_READ = ("PROGRESS_LOG.md",        # the log is append-only: what it said on
             # lock stays unread, because the lock plants the old forms to show that it sees them.
             "frontier/B1862_the_audits_first_corrections/verification/",
             "frontier/B1892_review_79_read_by_those_who_did_not_build_it/", "frontier/B1894_",      # the review's arcs quote what the readers found
-            "/verification/readers/")                            # a reader's report quotes what it found
+            "/verification/readers/",                            # a reader's report quotes what it found
+            # ADDED 2026-11-13 (the building session; the full suite on the tip of its deliveries since main's 0e637ea9e, where
+            # this test failed, and fails at main's head too): the rows of B1905 are six readers' rows, one an arc, each with a
+            # quotation of a verdict line as it stood at a15516d43, checked by machine at that commit.  They quote the old forms
+            # as the readers found them, as a reader's report does (main's hand-over copy left the tree with B1905, C13's first patch).
+            "frontier/B1905_selection_and_chirality_across_the_record/verification/rows.json.txt")
 HELD_BY_ITS_OWN_LOCK = {("papers/structure_paper/SKELETON.md", "E5")}      # the sentence is true there and held to the computation
 # this arc's page quotes two old forms in blocks that do not hold their correction (its table of what the audit found): as
 # found on 2026-11-12, by count, for each finding.  One more of either, or one of any other finding, is reported.
diff --git a/tests/test_ledger_of_walls.py b/tests/test_ledger_of_walls.py
index c2a087c85..34431a02c 100644
--- a/tests/test_ledger_of_walls.py
+++ b/tests/test_ledger_of_walls.py
@@ -106,5 +106,10 @@ def test_a_row_added_a_class_changed_and_a_word_of_the_outcome_changed_each_move
 
 
 def test_the_generator_leaves_nothing_beside_b1905s_script():
+    # CHANGED 2026-11-13 (the full suite on the tip): the line read
+    #     assert not (ARC / "verification" / "__pycache__").exists()
+    # and pytest itself writes that folder for the arc's lock, which stands in the same folder.  What the generator must not
+    # leave is a compiled copy of B1905's script; that is what is looked for.
     G._walls_source()
-    assert not (ARC / "verification" / "__pycache__").exists()
+    cache = ARC / "verification" / "__pycache__"
+    assert not (cache.exists() and any(f.name.startswith("sweep_tables") for f in cache.iterdir()))
